::ENG2_U04_L05_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Finding: A cafeteria manager explained that reminders helped more students complete the lunch form. Which sentence integrates the source best?{
~A. The manager said stuff.#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
=B. A cafeteria manager explained that reminders helped more students complete the lunch form after the first week.#Correct. This gives a source lead-in and clearly states the finding.
~C. Reminders did things.#Incorrect. This lacks precision.
~D. Forms are cool.#Incorrect. This is personal opinion.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which transition best signals contrast?{
~A. In addition#Incorrect. This adds information.
~B. For example#Incorrect. This introduces an example.
~C. Also#Incorrect. This adds information.
=D. However#Correct. This transition signals contrast or complication.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence has the most appropriate academic voice?{
=A. The pre-order form reduced unwanted trays when staff prepared meals from student selections.#Correct. This sentence is precise, formal, and evidence-based.
~B. The lunch form was totally awesome.#Incorrect. This is informal and exaggerated.
~C. The report said some stuff happened.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~D. Everybody should love forms.#Incorrect. This is biased.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best explains source evidence?{
~A. The report is a report.#Incorrect. This does not explain the evidence.
~B. It was about lunch.#Incorrect. This is too general.
=C. The evidence shows that meal preparation changed when staff used student selections, which helped reduce unwanted trays.#Correct. This explains how the evidence answers the research question.
~D. Forms are paper.#Incorrect. This is not the key finding.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which revision fixes the fragment: "Because reminders helped students complete the form."{
=A. Reminders helped students complete the form, which improved the routine.#Correct. This is a complete sentence.
~B. Students complete because reminders form.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~C. Because reminders helped students complete the form and.#Incorrect. This is still incomplete.
~D. Because reminders.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q06::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which lead-in best introduces a source?{
~A. Some stuff says#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. It was like#Incorrect. This is informal.
~C. Everybody knows#Incorrect. This is unsupported.
=D. A district report found#Correct. This identifies the source type and introduces evidence.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q07::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Source A gives a benefit. Source B adds a related support. Which transition best connects Source B?{
~A. However#Incorrect. This suggests contrast, not related support.
=B. In addition#Correct. This adds related source information.
~C. Instead#Incorrect. This suggests replacement.
~D. On the other hand#Incorrect. This suggests contrast.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q08::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Draft: "This report proves lunch forms fixed everything forever." Which revision is most accurate?{
~A. This report proves total perfection forever.#Incorrect. This still exaggerates.
~B. The report proves all cafeterias are solved.#Incorrect. This overstates the evidence.
=C. The report suggests that pre-order forms reduced unwanted trays during the pilot.#Correct. This is measured and source-based.
~D. Lunch forms are flawless.#Incorrect. This is exaggerated.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q09::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best combines source integration and explanation?{
~A. A report said trays.#Incorrect. This is incomplete and vague.
~B. Trays and forms happened.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~C. The evidence is good because good.#Incorrect. This does not explain the relationship.
=D. A district report found fewer unwanted trays after the pre-order pilot, showing that student selections helped staff prepare meals more accurately.#Correct. This integrates the source and explains the evidence.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q10::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence uses standard English punctuation?{
=A. A district report found that trays decreased after the pre-order pilot.#Correct. This sentence is punctuated correctly.
~B. A district report found, that trays decreased.#Incorrect. The comma is unnecessary after "found."
~C. A district report found that, trays decreased.#Incorrect. The comma interrupts the clause.
~D. A district report, found that trays decreased.#Incorrect. The comma separates the subject from the verb.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q11::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which transition best signals a result?{
~A. For example#Incorrect. This introduces an example.
~B. In contrast#Incorrect. This signals difference.
=C. As a result#Correct. This phrase signals an effect or outcome.
~D. Similarly#Incorrect. This signals similarity.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q12::[MLA.ENG2.RS.01] Which sentence uses source information responsibly?{
~A. The source says one pilot reduced trays, so every school will solve all waste forever.#Incorrect. This overgeneralizes.
=B. The source shows that one pre-order pilot reduced unwanted trays in its setting.#Correct. This stays within what the source supports.
~C. The source proves nothing can ever improve.#Incorrect. This contradicts the finding.
~D. The source should be ignored.#Incorrect. It provides relevant evidence.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q13::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which source integration is weakest?{
=A. The source thing said stuff was good.#Correct. This is vague and informal.
~B. A district report found that the pilot reduced unwanted trays.#Incorrect. This is clear source integration.
~C. A cafeteria manager explained that reminders improved form completion.#Incorrect. This is clear source integration.
~D. A teacher guide noted that journals helped students track observations.#Incorrect. This clearly identifies source and finding.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q14::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best improves tone? Original: "Only careless students forgot the form."{
~A. Only really careless students forgot the form.#Incorrect. This still attacks students.
~B. Students were awful at forms.#Incorrect. This is biased.
~C. Nobody can remember anything.#Incorrect. This is exaggerated.
=D. Some students needed reminders to complete the form during the first week.#Correct. This uses objective, evidence-based wording.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q15::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best introduces a limitation?{
~A. The program was perfect.#Incorrect. This ignores limitations.
~B. There were no problems ever.#Incorrect. This is inaccurate and exaggerated.
=C. However, some students needed reminders during the first week.#Correct. "However" introduces a challenge or limitation.
~D. In addition, there was no challenge.#Incorrect. This does not introduce a limitation.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q16::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is clearest?{
~A. Report trays because students selections.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
=B. The report connects fewer unwanted trays to meal preparation based on student selections.#Correct. This is clear and complete.
~C. Because selections trays.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~D. The report, the trays, the students.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q17::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best uses a purposeful transition?{
~A. However, the report and also and.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~B. In contrast, the same source adds the same idea.#Incorrect. "In contrast" does not fit if the idea is the same.
=C. However, the first week showed that students needed reminders to complete the form.#Correct. "However" accurately signals a challenge.
~D. As a result, here is a definition.#Incorrect. This does not show a result.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q18::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence best revises for an academic audience?{
=A. The cafeteria manager explained that reminders helped more students complete the form.#Correct. This is formal and precise.
~B. The manager was like, reminders helped.#Incorrect. This is informal.
~C. The manager said form stuff.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~D. Reminders were awesome.#Incorrect. This is informal.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q19::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence needs more explanation after source evidence?{
~A. This finding matters because it shows the preparation process reduced waste.#Incorrect. This is explanation.
=B. A district report found that the pilot reduced unwanted trays.#Correct. This integrates evidence, but it should be followed by explanation of why it matters.
~C. The finding connects to the research question about food waste.#Incorrect. This explains relevance.
~D. Therefore, student selections helped staff prepare meals more accurately.#Incorrect. This explains the relationship.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q20::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which pair best shows source integration plus transition?{
~A. "Stuff happened. Also stuff."#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. "The source said something, and yeah."#Incorrect. This is not academic.
~C. "Forms are cool. Reports are there."#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
=D. "A district report found that unwanted trays decreased. In addition, a cafeteria manager explained that reminders improved form completion."#Correct. This pair integrates both sources and uses a transition.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q21::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which wording is most precise?{
=A. reduced unwanted trays#Correct. This phrase is specific and evidence-based.
~B. was really good#Incorrect. This is too general.
~C. made lunch better somehow#Incorrect. This is vague.
~D. fixed stuff#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q22::[MLA.ENG2.RS.01] Which statement best keeps source meaning accurate? Source: Reminders helped more students complete the form after the first week.{
~A. Students never needed reminders.#Incorrect. This contradicts the source.
~B. Reminders made forms unnecessary.#Incorrect. The source does not say that.
=C. Reminders improved form completion after the first week.#Correct. This accurately restates the source.
~D. Students completed no forms.#Incorrect. This contradicts the source.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q23::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence has a tone problem?{
~A. The report found fewer unwanted trays.#Incorrect. This is neutral.
~B. The manager explained that reminders helped.#Incorrect. This is neutral.
~C. The pilot reduced waste in one setting.#Incorrect. This is measured.
=D. Only foolish students forgot the form.#Correct. This attacks students and creates biased tone.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q24::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best explains a contrast between benefit and challenge?{
~A. The pilot reduced trays and reduced trays.#Incorrect. This repeats one idea.
=B. The pilot reduced unwanted trays; however, some students needed reminders at first.#Correct. This sentence uses a transition to connect benefit and challenge.
~C. The form thing was great.#Incorrect. This is informal and lacks contrast.
~D. Students are students.#Incorrect. This does not explain a contrast.
}

::ENG2_U04_L05_Q25::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which checklist best matches Lesson 5 writing?{
=A. Source lead-in, accurate evidence, explanation, purposeful transition, academic voice.#Correct. These are the key Lesson 5 skills.
~B. Vague source mention, no explanation, casual wording.#Incorrect. This would weaken the writing.
~C. Opinion only with no sources.#Incorrect. The lesson requires source integration.
~D. Random transitions and copied evidence only.#Incorrect. Transitions must match meaning and evidence must be explained.
}
